  "issues": [],
  "result": "NO_CONFIRMED_ACTIONABLE_DEFECT_FOUND_IN_REVIEWED_SOURCE",
  "reasoning": [
    {
      "area": "Real owner and saved shape",
      "evidence": [
        "meta_store/remembered_pages.rs validate_owner checks sessions.id+created_at under the metadata mutex/transaction; unsafe/new draft caller receives no synthetic owner.",
        "SavedPages has deny_unknown_fields and only version/createdAt/revision/items; item fields only id/url. No grants/native labels/snapshot/title stored.",
        "Frontend ownerForRememberedPages consumes a real matching established index row; backend does not rely on a draft owner claim."
      ],
      "limits": "Static review of this source slice; no installed/native verification."
    },
    {
      "area": "CAS and atomically persisted deletion",
      "evidence": [
        "remember_page/forget_page use SQLite immediate transactions for read-owner/read-list/check-revision/write/commit. Distinct connections cannot both commit the same baseline revision.",
        "Even clearing an already-empty list persists incremented revision, preventing stale CAS0 resurrection. Duplicate remember leaves same list without writes.",
        "remove_session now deletes session+exact browserPages key in the same transaction; a descriptor cleanup error rolls back session deletion. session_delete propagates removal failure."
      ],
      "limits": "The pre-existing remove_session then dismiss_session facade still uses two separate transactions; this review does not promote it to an atomic entire remote-delete/tombstone transaction."
    },
    {
      "area": "Page confirmation and caller boundary",
      "evidence": [
        "All four IPC commands call require_main from actual Webview context.",
        "Remember holds browser operation serialization and Browser Store mutex through the short metadata commit; selected label, page revision, task/session key, complete current URL, ready/error-free state and public-vs-local/preview classification all checked.",
        "Selected-page predicate excludes shutdown, close, withdrawing, incomplete creation and selection switching.",
        "A-B-A invalidates old page revision; URL/path/query/fragment must match complete current canonical URL.",
        "Public URL admission rejects known login/auth/secret markers and local targets; exact URL normalization enforced before persistence."
      ],
      "limits": "Known-marker URL admission cannot prove arbitrary opaque path/query has no secret. Explicit per-page user non-secret confirmation remains necessary; source/tests do not establish its installed UX."
    },
    {
      "area": "Late reopen cleanup and owner retention",
      "evidence": [
        "Reopen uses current list CAS/item lookup, performs fresh public view reserve/create and re-verifies actual owner afterward.",
        "Deletion/clear during native creation triggers close_owned of the exact new task/label. A confirmed close returns the owner error; unknown close returns actual retained BrowserInfo rather than abandoning identity.",
        "close_owned marks closing, revokes lease, awaits sharing stop then exact native close ACK; failure preserves error owner and retry identity.",
        "reserve creates a fresh page/read lease; descriptor does not select/ready/authorize the new page or restore an old read grant."
      ],
      "limits": "Forget descriptor intentionally does not close/revoke an already requested/live page. Native missing-ACK behavior examined in source and controlled tests, not exercised by this reviewer."
    },
    {
      "area": "Clear, readonly, corrupt data and resource limits",
      "evidence": [
        "Existing clear_all deletes records and seals query_only while holding the same metadata mutex; pending remembered writers cannot rewrite deleted old owner.",
        "Corrupt/future/extra-field/owner-mismatched/oversize/duplicate/unsafe-url saved payloads return errors before write/forget and retain original value.",
        "100 items, 1MiB saved payload and JavaScript-safe revisions bound parsed data and cross-language integers."
      ],
      "limits": "No disk full/power-loss or externally corrupted live database execution by this reviewer."
    },
    {
      "area": "Lock order and awaits",
      "evidence": [
        "remember: async Browser operation mutex -> blocking closure -> Browser Store mutex -> MetaStore mutex/SQLite; MetaStore.run itself does not pre-acquire metadata lock.",
        "New metadata methods only call pure URL policy; no MetaStore->Browser Store inverse path found in this slice.",
        "No std::MutexGuard is held across an await. Reopen metadata lookup/check and native create/close await sequentially under only the async operation lock.",
        "Run-event shutdown does not await the async operation lock, avoiding main-loop deadlock on native ACK."
      ],
      "limits": "No concurrency stress or runtime stall measurements were executed."
    }
  ],
  "counterexampleAttempts": [
    {
      "trace": "Save claimed URL for nonexistent/stale createdAt owner",
      "disposition": "Rejected by validate_owner within transaction; stale saved createdAt also invalid."
    },
    {
      "trace": "Confirm A then A-B-A or navigate before remember admission",
      "disposition": "Rejected by selected page and revision/fullURL checks; existing begin_select increments old page revision."
    },
    {
      "trace": "Forget empty list then late expectedRevision0 remember",
      "disposition": "Persistent revision advances; stale expected rejected."
    },
    {
      "trace": "Clear data or delete/recreate same id during create",
      "disposition": "Post-create owner verification rejects missing/different-createdAt owner; exact new view close attempt retains unknown owner. A new explicit confirmation for a new valid owner is not a stale old request."
    },
    {
      "trace": "Native creation timeout then owner deleted and close unconfirmed",
      "disposition": "Reserved page error identity remains, close_failed retains identity; finish_reopen returns that identity. No falsely acknowledged cleanup found."
    },
    {
      "trace": "Overwrite a corrupt record by remember or forget",
      "disposition": "read validates shape before both writes; error returns preserve old row."
    },
    {
      "trace": "Metadata mutex inverted with Browser Store mutex",
      "disposition": "No inverse path in the added code and direct metadata dependencies; pure URL validation does not lock Browser Store."
    }
  ],
  "verificationBoundary": "No confirmed issue is not proof of overall correctness. Owner is running the sole relevant cargo/fmt/clippy checks; reviewer did not duplicate those commands. Native install/UI, cancellation schedules and all-Agent claims remain separate."
